--- RUN 1b raw serial: q35 + nvme + intel-iommu + igb (VT-d) ---
 69: [ WARN] [vtd] Intel VT-d: DMA isolation ACTIVE (per-Cell domains, Sv39 SLPT)
154: [ WARN] [vtd] Cell 3 BDF 00:02.0 DID=1 SLPT=0x14a000 phys=0x833000 size=0x1000
184: [ WARN] [vtd] Cell 4 BDF 00:1f.2 DID=2 SLPT=0x14e000 phys=0xfa5000 size=0x1000
304: USER: [igb] controller bound 8086:10c9 82576 (QEMU model) link_up=true mac=52:54:00:12:34:56
305: [ WARN] [driver_cell] NIC driver registered: tid=8
306: USER: [net-bridge] first e1000 TX len=304 accepted=true
308: USER: [net-bridge] first e1000 RX len=590
314: USER: [net] DHCP acquired — IP configured
315: USER: [net] IP address: 10.0.2.15

Ordering asserted by the lane: isolation ACTIVE (69) precedes the igb bind (304)
precedes registration (305) < Tx (306) < Rx (308) < DHCP (314) < leased address
(315). Cell 3 is BDF 00:02.0 — the igb controller — so its descriptor and buffer
DMA ran under a per-device domain (DID=1) with explicit SLPT mappings, not
untranslated. Cell 4 is the NVMe endpoint (00:1f.2, DID=2).

Identity assertions hold in both runs: the sibling `/bin/e1000` cell emits no
`[e1000]` line at all (it no longer matches the shared Ethernet class triple),
`[e1000] unsupported Ethernet 8086:10c9` is absent, and no syscall is denied for
the igb cell.

