--------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope (A-01)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
The VT-d variant is a q35 gate. QEMU's vIOMMU tables are QEMU-generated, not
firmware DMAR, so the parser's firmware path is only fully exercised in phase 07.
The `x86_64-pc` descriptor refuses the q35 register-base fallback by design, so a
GenericX86Pc lane image cannot serve this variant until phase 05 discovers the
base from ACPI DMAR. QEMU's `igb` model is 82576-class; it does not model the
i210/i211 iNVM or PHY, so nothing here is evidence for those parts.
